Count the frames dropped because the decode unit queue overflowed (the overflowing frame, the
queued frames flushed with it and every whole frame dropped until the IDR frame it requested) apart
from network loss, so the performance overlay, the stream doctor and the bitrate logic no longer
read a decoder that fell behind as frame loss (nightjar#80; LiGetDecoderDrops, the Rust engine's
VideoStats::decoder_drops). A frame lost or abandoned meanwhile stays network loss. Add it at the
end of the list.

